# What the alias distribution ships.
#
# `vdi2770-validate` is two lines that make the old import name the same object
# as `vdi2770.validate`. The rules, the schema, the corpus, the tools and the
# suite all live in `vdi2770` now and travel in its sdist — shipping them here
# would put a copy of the tool inside a distribution that contains none of it,
# and the tests would run against whatever happened to be installed nearby.
# That is the borrowed green result this repository publishes two sdists to
# avoid.
include LICENSE NOTICE CHANGELOG.md CONTRIBUTING.md SECURITY.md README-vdi2770-validate.md
# `prune`, explicitly. Setuptools adds a default set of its own on top of what
# is named here, and `tests/` is in it — the sdist carried seventy-three test
# files for a distribution containing none of the code they test, which the
# gate below noticed and this line answers.
prune tests
prune tools
prune corpus
prune docs
prune packages
# Working notes are not part of the distribution.
exclude CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md
prune .claude
